{"schema": "http://ihsn.org/schemas/timeseries-db", "schema_version": "0.0.1", "type": "timeseries-db", "idno": "9405b079-4f15-4827-930e-29adea8879b1", "changed": "1762558231", "changed_utc": "2025-11-07T18:30:31-05:00", "created": "1740604258", "created_utc": "2025-02-26T16:10:58-05:00", "created_by": "91", "changed_by": "4", "database_description": {"title_statement": {"idno": "IMF_FFS", "title": "Fossil Fuel Subsidies"}, "abstract": "The extent to which fossil fuel prices paid by consumers do not reflect the fuels' full financial and social costs, expressed as an aggregate value for each fuel and economy.\n\nUndercharging for fuels is disaggregated into explicit and implicit subsidies. Explicit subsidies measure the amount that the financial cost to supply a fuel (i.e., the supply cost) exceeds the price paid by the fuel user. Implicit subsidies measure the difference between a fuel's full social cost and the price paid by the fuel user, exclusive of any explicit subsidy. A fuel's full social cost includes both supply costs and negative externalities, which are costs imposed on society due to consuming the fuel and primarily include local air pollution, climate change, and broader externalities related to driving.\n\nIt should be noted that the concept of \"subsidies\" used here differs from the definition of subsidies in macroeconomic statistics.\n\nFor further details, please refer to https://climatedata.imf.org/datasets/d48cfd2124954fb0900cef95f2db2724_0/about", "license": [{"note": "Permission is required to copy or download IMF Content in any systematic way or to re-use, publish, and disseminate a substantial amount beyond \u201cFair Use,\u201d whether for commercial or noncommercial purposes.\u00a0.\nFor more information see https://www.imf.org/en/About/copyright-and-terms#data.", "name": "License Specified Externally"}], "authoring_entity": [{"name": "International Monetary Fund (IMF)", "uri": "https://www.imf.org/"}], "url": "https://climatedata.imf.org/pages/mitigation/#mi3", "topics": [{"id": "P4", "name": "Infrastructure", "vocabulary": "WB Practice Groups", "uri": "https://fmr.worldbank.org/FMR/sdmx/v2/structure/codelist/WB.DATA360/CL_D360_TOPICS/1.0"}, {"id": "P4_000001", "name": "Energy & Extractives", "parent_id": "P4", "vocabulary": "Data360 Topic L1", "uri": "https://fmr.worldbank.org/FMR/sdmx/v2/structure/hierarchy/WB.DATA360/H_D360_TOPICS/1.0"}, {"id": "P4_000007", "name": "Energy Markets, Planning and Trade", "parent_id": "P4_000001", "vocabulary": "Data360 Topic L2", "uri": "https://fmr.worldbank.org/FMR/sdmx/v2/structure/hierarchy/WB.DATA360/H_D360_TOPICS/1.0"}], "version": [{"version": "1.0", "date": "2025-03-09"}], "time_coverage": [{"start": "2015", "end": "2030"}], "ref_country": [{"name": "Afghanistan", "code": "AFG"}, {"name": "Albania", "code": "ALB"}, {"name": "Algeria", "code": "DZA"}, {"name": "Angola", "code": "AGO"}, {"name": "Argentina", "code": "ARG"}, {"name": "Armenia", "code": "ARM"}, {"name": "Australia", "code": "AUS"}, {"name": "Austria", "code": "AUT"}, {"name": "Azerbaijan", "code": "AZE"}, {"name": "Bahamas, The", "code": "BHS"}, {"name": "Bahrain", "code": "BHR"}, {"name": "Bangladesh", "code": "BGD"}, {"name": "Barbados", "code": "BRB"}, {"name": "Belarus", "code": "BLR"}, {"name": "Belgium", "code": "BEL"}, {"name": "Belize", "code": "BLZ"}, {"name": "Benin", "code": "BEN"}, {"name": "Bhutan", "code": "BTN"}, {"name": "Bolivia", "code": "BOL"}, {"name": "Bosnia and Herzegovina", "code": "BIH"}, {"name": "Botswana", "code": "BWA"}, {"name": "Brazil", "code": "BRA"}, {"name": "Brunei Darussalam", "code": "BRN"}, {"name": "Bulgaria", "code": "BGR"}, {"name": "Burkina Faso", "code": "BFA"}, {"name": "Burundi", "code": "BDI"}, {"name": "Cabo Verde", "code": "CPV"}, {"name": "Cambodia", "code": "KHM"}, {"name": "Cameroon", "code": "CMR"}, {"name": "Canada", "code": "CAN"}, {"name": "Central African Republic", "code": "CAF"}, {"name": "Chad", "code": "TCD"}, {"name": "Chile", "code":